A||||2||mbramble||Took a Little Trip||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||10-31-2000||09:01 AM||||Drove the Fiero (87 2.5L Coupe) from Pensacola to Jupiter, FL on Thursday and back on Sun night.  1400 miles round trip.<P>It ran beautifully!!  Got about 33 MPG overall for the trip but drove 80+ MPH for most of the trip.  In fact, for most of the trip my 85MPH speedo needle was buried!!  Didn't use a drop of oil.  Was 'using' a bit before I realised the bolts for my valve cover were barely finger tight a couple weeks ago!!  Replaced the gasket and tightened it down and haven't lost any oil since. <P>It was a pretty comfortable drive.  My son drove a couple of hours but I did the rest.  The sunroof was a great addition, as were the power windows and mirrors. I tend to shift around in the seat quite a bit after a few hours of driving and the mirrors are now a snap to adjust when I do so.<P>We were able to get all his baseball gear, clothes, pillows, etc., in the car with not a square inch to spare...<P>On the trip we saw 3 Fieros -- all in/around Jupiter. One yellow one at a college adjoining the Jupiter stadium; what looked to be a silver 85 GT delivering pizzas to the hotel!! (we saw him from the 3rd floor and he was gone before we got downstairs), and a white 87 coupe on I95 at exit 56 (where the ballpark is).  Driven by a very nice looking woman.  We drove up beside, beeped, she waved, and then we had to turn off for the ballpark....<P>It was a great trip.  I now feel confident to drive the car anywhere.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||10:31 AM||||I love to drive my Fiero on long trips. Up east it is getting to that time for my Fiero to settle in for the long winter nap. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I will miss it all winter.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-31-2000||11:12 AM||||Mine got taken off the road Saturday.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Pulled the seats out to do some maintance (replace a seat belt holder)and replace a seat cover.  I turn the plates in and keep minimal insurance on it until March, when it goes back on the road. ||||reg||9
